WEBVTT

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:04.400
All of us are at least 20 years old!

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:09.980
This here is the sales promotion service
our company currently offers.

00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:12.990
What an incredible idea!

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:15.110
We would love to incorporate your services!

00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:18.410
This will absolutely be a hit!
Our company is safe in your hands!

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:20.410
I've already gone ahead and procured funding for it!

00:00:31.670 --> 00:00:34.010
Oh what...? It was all a dream?

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:11.440
Michiru Amatsuki was on the
verge of crisis.

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:12.980
A presentation?!

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:18.950
One of our clients contacted us about providing
some new ideas for sales promotion tools.

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:24.910
And since I wanted to incorporate them into our new plan anyway, I want you to go pitch it to them.

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:27.370
But I've never even given a presentation before...

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:30.750
Well there's a first time for everything!
It'll be a good experience for you.

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:35.250
This is one of our closest clients. They won't give you
a hassle for tripping over your words a bit.

00:02:36.130 --> 00:02:38.550
<i>So that's what you expect of me, huh...?</i>

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:42.260
<i>Which brings us to today!</i>

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:43.810
I'm Michiru Amatsuki!

00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:46.060
Thanks for gathering here today!

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:47.770
I made it through my first line!

00:02:47.770 --> 00:02:49.810
Your mic is switched off.

00:02:49.810 --> 00:02:50.770
What?!

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:52.860
S-sorry about that...

00:02:56.150 --> 00:03:00.070
<i>Well I made it through I guess, but that was a mess...</i>

00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:03.780
1 new message

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:07.950
We just got word back about today's pitch!

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:09.000
What's it say?

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:11.710
"After careful discussion of your services
among our staff here..."

00:03:11.710 --> 00:03:14.790
"We wish to take you up on your service."

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:18.130
That's a new contract for you, Amatsuki-san!

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:18.800
What?

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:21.590
That's the client you're in charge of is it not?

00:03:21.590 --> 00:03:23.800
Congrats on a successful pitch.

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:26.850
Sir, I think we might have broken Amatsuki-san!

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:32.520
Making good progress like this puts you up
for appraisal and earns you a bigger bonus.

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:34.810
Okay, she's not completely frozen.

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:39.780
<i>It still doesn't even feel real...</i>

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:42.320
<i>But I really did it!</i>

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:45.320
Oh! Michiru-chan!

00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:49.830
So you landed a new deal?

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:51.830
Nice work, Michiru!

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:54.080
You really worked hard at this one.

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:55.790
Thank you both.

00:03:55.790 --> 00:03:58.840
Well, this calls for a celebration!

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:00.340
Hope you're ready for some drinks!

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:01.670
C'mon over and have a seat!

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:04.590
She's only happy to have an excuse to drink!

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:12.600
A gift from the customer right over here.

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:15.190
Suntory Whisky Kakubin?

00:04:15.190 --> 00:04:19.280
I, Nao Kiriyama, am about
to honor you with a highball, Michiru!

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:23.280
First you get a nice big glass and fill it with ice.

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:25.870
Then, you mix in 1 part whisky with 4 parts soda water.

00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:28.870
Squeeze a little lemon in there and it gets even better!

00:04:28.870 --> 00:04:32.870
Be ever so gentle with the soda so it doesn't go flat.

00:04:32.870 --> 00:04:34.870
Then mix it up real carefully.

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:37.960
And you've got yourself a kaku-highball!

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:39.250
Go on then!

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:49.510
I sealed the deal!

00:04:49.510 --> 00:04:51.640
Congratulations!

00:04:51.640 --> 00:04:53.850
Here's a little present from me then.

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:57.400
Don't tell me that bag you're fondling there is...!

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:00.400
It is! I knew it!

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:01.860
Some chicken karaage!

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:04.530
There has never been such a perfect match!

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:08.370
Yowch!

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:11.790
They're still so hot and juicy!

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:16.420
Is there anything closer to pure bliss,
than a freshly deep fried karaage?

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:19.420
They're so good I don't even care about
burning my mouth off!

00:05:19.420 --> 00:05:25.010
Once your mouth is all coated with that oily chicken,
take your kaku-highball and...

00:05:28.510 --> 00:05:32.310
It really brings out that sweet flavor
of the soda and whisky!

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:34.140
Why are they such a perfect match?

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:36.190
The thing with Kakubin you see...

00:05:36.190 --> 00:05:40.770
Is that it's a whisky blended
specifically to be mixed with soda!

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:42.320
No way!

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:45.480
It's been on the market for more than 70 years,

00:05:45.490 --> 00:05:49.200
tweaking the blend to match the times!

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:52.580
But the bottle itself looks the same as always, huh?

00:05:52.580 --> 00:05:54.910
That's just another stunning fact about it!

00:05:54.910 --> 00:05:59.580
Kakubin was the very first whisky
made by Japan for Japan.

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:05.300
And the tortoise-shell like design
of the bottle comes from Satsuma kiriko works!

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:07.840
I never realized it was supposed to look like a shell!

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:12.350
The generations may change,
but concepts like these carry through the ages!

00:06:12.350 --> 00:06:15.100
The fact that it's been
so popular for so long is impressive!

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:17.350
It's got the life span... of a tortoise!

00:06:17.350 --> 00:06:19.960
Where on Earth did you get that...?

00:06:22.610 --> 00:06:23.730
Amatsuki-san.

00:06:23.730 --> 00:06:24.530
Yes?

00:06:24.530 --> 00:06:25.360
I wanted to ask you about-

00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:27.700
Amatsuki-san, you've got a call
from the planning department.

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:29.860
I-I'll call them back!

00:06:29.860 --> 00:06:33.330
Amatsuki-san, when you finish your meeting,
there's something I want to ask, so just let me know.

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:34.740
R-right, yeah...

00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:40.080
I've suddenly been handed
so much responsibility that I can't keep up...

00:06:45.380 --> 00:06:48.090
But if I don't keep up...

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:53.600
Amatsuki-san sure has been hard at work.

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:56.810
She seems a bit overworked to me though.

00:06:57.980 --> 00:07:00.810
A full stomach has my body begging for a nap...

00:07:01.190 --> 00:07:04.020
<i>We've got a celebration later tonight and all so...</i>

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:07.740
<i>Maybe I'll just nap a bit until the meeting this afternoon...</i>

00:07:15.030 --> 00:07:17.700
It's 1:30! The meeting's already started!

00:07:17.700 --> 00:07:20.710
Sorry! Sorry! So sorry! So-!

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:25.210
Amatsuki-san, good work today.

00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:27.380
Hanamori-san...

00:07:27.380 --> 00:07:29.130
Don't you think you're overdoing it a bit?

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:32.930
But this is all stuff I'm supposed to be in charge of...

00:07:32.930 --> 00:07:36.310
If you don't wrap up soon though,
you won't make it in time for our celebration today.

00:07:36.310 --> 00:07:38.060
Let's just call it quits here for the day.

00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:40.940
We can't go celebrating your success
without you around, you know.

00:07:40.940 --> 00:07:42.850
But I'm not...

00:07:42.850 --> 00:07:44.940
What do you have left?

00:07:44.940 --> 00:07:49.490
I need to at least send out a sales slip
and write up a daily report...

00:07:53.360 --> 00:07:54.370
That's that!

00:07:54.370 --> 00:07:55.490
So fast...!

00:07:55.490 --> 00:07:58.990
So here goes, to our latest sale!

00:07:58.990 --> 00:08:01.000
Cheers!

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:02.830
Hey, so did you hear that guy's getting married?

00:08:02.830 --> 00:08:03.920
What? No way.

00:08:07.880 --> 00:08:10.920
What's with that long face there, Amatsuki?

00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:13.800
I'm so slow at work.

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:17.510
I envy how fast you are. A true pro...

00:08:19.270 --> 00:08:23.190
It just takes time. I've been at this for 5 years now.

00:08:25.860 --> 00:08:29.860
I mean when I first joined,
I was messing things up all the time.

00:08:29.860 --> 00:08:36.820
Heck, I almost lost a 10 million yen contract over a little mistake and nearly sent our boss's head rolling.

00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:40.290
Didn't that wear you down...?

00:08:40.290 --> 00:08:42.040
Of course it did.

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:46.040
I even thought it might be better
for the company if I quit, but...

00:08:47.540 --> 00:08:49.460
Hanamori-san.

00:08:49.460 --> 00:08:50.590
Who- Wha-?!

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:54.010
We still managed to wrangle that deal in,
so don't worry about it.

00:08:54.010 --> 00:08:55.300
Is that you, Boss?

00:08:55.300 --> 00:08:58.180
We need our young employees to be like tortoises.

00:08:58.180 --> 00:09:01.310
Is that the look you were going for...?

00:09:01.310 --> 00:09:06.400
He told me us tortoises need to just keep focused
on working towards our goals.

00:09:06.400 --> 00:09:10.150
Rather than worry about how we can't
keep up with the faster rabbits.

00:09:10.150 --> 00:09:15.110
So quit worrying about how fast you get things done,
and let's just focus on getting it done!

00:09:15.610 --> 00:09:16.780
Tortoises, huh...?

00:09:20.950 --> 00:09:23.700
I-I'll take a kaku-highball too!

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:26.460
Oh, looks like someone's in a better mood!

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:32.590
Hanamori-san, thanks for that.

00:09:32.590 --> 00:09:34.130
Yeah, keep up the good work!

00:09:38.470 --> 00:09:40.350
Good morning!

00:09:40.350 --> 00:09:42.470
Good morning, Amatsuki-san.

00:09:42.470 --> 00:09:43.970
Sir!

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:49.980
I, Michiru Amatsuki, have accepted myself as a tortoise!

00:09:49.980 --> 00:09:52.650
Uh... right...

00:09:57.490 --> 00:10:00.950
Let's just move along on this schedule, then.

00:10:00.950 --> 00:10:02.990
I look forward to working with you!

00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:07.000
Whew. All this and it's still only Monday!

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:09.880
But it looks like this could go well.

00:10:15.510 --> 00:10:18.930
<i>Turtles and tortoises
are pretty much the same thing, right?</i>

00:10:18.930 --> 00:10:20.640
<i>I wonder if this actually works...</i>

00:10:21.100 --> 00:10:25.520
<i>There's still a long way to go,
but I'll just take things one step at a time!</i>

00:12:01.110 --> 00:12:05.700
The name Kakubin is just what people
started calling based on the shape of the bottle itself.

00:12:06.200 --> 00:12:12.710
Well, I wouldn't mind if people will ever
just start calling me Sexy Dynamite Kae.

00:12:12.920 --> 00:12:15.380
Here's to another night!
